wajo21_q7.solution:
Since each poor person gets 2 vegetables, the number of poor people is half the total number of vegetables. So there are<br>$$
(86+47+93) / 2=113 \text{ poor people. }
$$<br>Of these people, 86 get a potato and something else.<br>Hence, the remaining $113-86=27$ people each get a carrot and a parsnip.
